irmed broken first-party imports [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]introduced by combining concurrent commits, while keeping [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]unchanged-base landings cheap and checker failures bounded and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]fail-open.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]rebased_stitch_gate.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/rebased_stitch_gate.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/task_backlog_epic_1.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1pm.5.1[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1pm/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase-1pm.5.1.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Define the shared rebase gate contract in Rust[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-policy[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-policy: implement shared gate policy in sase-core, expose and test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its Python bindings, and add the thin sase adapter. Own eligibility, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]changed-path union, pending-context merging, and verdict validation. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Keep the gate disabled.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Execute configurable rebase hooks with a hard deadline[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-runner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-policy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-runner: implement project-scoped configuration, bounded process [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]execution and evidence, fail-open errors, default configuration, schema,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and hook documentation. Do not 